WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.767
We're about to play a game
called "Box of Lies,"

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.367
but I'm going to need some help.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.934
She is this week's musical guest
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:09.100
and her album
"Red (Taylor's Version)"

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.901
is out at midnight tonight.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:13.667
Please welcome Taylor Swift!

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:20.133
♪♪

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.367
-Hello.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.534
-[ Chuckles ]
Thank you so much for --

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.534
Taylor, get ready to play --

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.801
We've never played this game,
have we?

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.300
-We have not played this game.
-No, we've played

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.834
a bunch of games,
but this one is a new one.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.501
Here we go.
Now, here's how it works.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:34.234
We have nine mystery boxes
containing objects

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.801
no one has ever seen before.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.467
On your turn, you pick a box.
Take out the object.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.234
Describe the object
to your opponent, okay?

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.534
And they have to guess if you're
lying or telling the truth.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:45.267
We'll play three rounds.

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.267
I mean, and, you know,

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.667
I'm not that good
of an actor, so...

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:50.100
-That's ridiculous.
Don't say things like that.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.234
That's your first lie.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.701
Immediately know.

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:56.167
-Why don't you choose
the first box?

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.934
Any one. Any number you'd like.
-Okay.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.901
-[ Humming ]

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.934
Oh, number one. Okay.

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.634
-Big shock.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:05.734
Oh, look at this.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:08.167
Not that heavy,
so that's the first hint.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.968
All right. Here we go. Yeah.

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:11.434
-[ Gasps ]

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:13.801
-[ Chuckles ]
-Oh, my God.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.334
-Uh-huh.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.567
-Where do I put it?

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.901
-You can put it
here in the front.

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.901
I won't see it.
Are you going to lie to me...

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:29.167
or are you going to tell
the truth, Taylor Swift?

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.667
-I don't have to lie because
I'm very excited to tell you

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:34.767
that it is
a "Wizards of Waverly Place" DVD

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:38.334
with a weird ribbon around it
that says, "I see corn."

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.868
-So specific.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.667
It sounds like something
our writers would do,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.267
but then you're delivering it
very innocent.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:48.767
Which makes me think that
you're maybe...making it up.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:51.934
Now you're laughing that I said
you're making it up.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:54.267
-I could be doing
a double bluff.

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:55.701
-All right.
I'm just going to say it.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:58.767
Taylor Swift, you are...

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.601
telling the truth.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:01.734
-I lied!

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:03.100
-[ Buzzer ]
-Aah!

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.033
Come on!

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.300
Oh, my God.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.667
-I lied.
-You lied.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:09.834
You did it.
-I lied.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.667
-Oh, my God.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.701
-I have a binoculars set
with corn stuffed in it.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.868
It's very upsetting.
It has baby corn at the top.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.000
It's bad.
-I'm sorry.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.601
-You should have known
I was lying

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:22.367
because I will do anything
to bring up Selena Gomez.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.634
Anything!

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:27.033
-I want to --
It's my turn to pick.

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:28.400
Which number shall I pick?

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.000
[ Audience shouting ]

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.801
Here we go.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:35.767
[ Grunting ]

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:39.000
-Ah. Okay. This is excellent.
This is really rough.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.367
What's happening over here?

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.133
Okay.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.868
-[ Panting ] Okay.

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:46.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.067
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:54.734
Where -- Where do I begin?

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.701
Uh...

00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:58.601
-It's a good one.
-Yeah.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:02:59.834
-Yeah.

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:03.567
-It's a family of pinecones
playing "Trouble."

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.200
-The game?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.267
-No. The song.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:10.701
-It'd be relevant.
-"I Knew You Were Trouble."

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.367
It would be relevant for "Red."
-It would be relevant.

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:14.467
-That's what I'm feeling.
-I just didn't know if they had

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.400
the sheet music for it
or something.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.467
-Whatever it is, it's odd.
It's weird and it's real.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.734
Or am I lying?

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:25.467
-Um, well, maybe you're telling
the truth about the pinecone...

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:28.467
-♪ Trouble, trouble, trouble ♪

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.033
-Okay.

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:32.901
[ Drum roll ]

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:35.067
You tell the truth.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.434
-[ Buzzer ]
-I got you!

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.834
-Oh, my God!

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:42.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.267
Oh, my God.

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.467
-Ahh!

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:50.234
[ Giggling ] Whoo! Whoo!

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.634
That felt good.
Man, I'm exhausted.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:52.968
-That was amazing.
You should be.

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:54.467
-I don't act.
I don't know how to act.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.968
-No, you do.
-Don't know how to act.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.200
-Either that, or we're, like,
the worst poker players,

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.300
the worst -- We should never --
We shouldn't be allowed outside.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.100
-We really shouldn't
be allowed outside.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.434
-Too gullible.
-We're too gullible.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:05.601
-Yeah.
-But you know what?

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.133
But here we go.
This is the last one.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:08.767
This is for all the marbles
right here.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.334
-Yeah.
-Taylor, you're up. Here we go.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.067
Come on. Which one?

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:16.200
Three? All right.
I'm not looking.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.834
Not looking. Not looking.

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:20.100
Not hearing. Not listening.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.200
We can still make noise.
So I don't cheat.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.300
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-I don't know what's happening.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.767
-Okay.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:31.601
♪♪

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.934
I've got in my vision...

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:35.634
um, a book.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:40.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.234
A b-- A book called, um,

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:47.934
"I'm Not Loving It: My Life
Under the Golden Arches,"

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:51.467
and it looks like it's
a biography written by, um...

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:52.868
-Ray Kroc?

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:59.067
-...by a fuzzy monster
with, um, seal hands.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:02.567
Um, it says
it's written by Grimace.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:05.734
Is that -- Is that -- Is that
a spokesperson for something?

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:07.033
-It's very famous.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.801
Grimace is very --
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.701
You're very young, Taylor.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.200
But, yes, Grimace is giant.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.200
We don't know really
what Grimace was.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.634
Is he purple where you are?

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.033
-It's actually
a black-and-white cover.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.100
It's a very serious book.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.667
Um, inside the book, it's --

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:24.968
You know how you can cut out
the pages of a book?

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:26.434
-Sure. I know that.

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:29.434
-Yeah, there's French fries
and a hamburger in here.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:31.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:40.100
♪♪

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.067
-Wow!

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.033
Taylor Swift...

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:47.834
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.133
You tell the truth.

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.000
-I do.
-Yes!

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:55.200
♪♪

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.000
-Oh, my gosh! Taylor Swift!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.334
That was stressful. Oh, my gosh.

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:04.067
I have to take -- I'm taking
that home, by the way.

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:05.334
You can take that home.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:07.000
-It smells delicious.
-You can have that.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.968
Yeah. You can have that.
Taylor Swift, everybody.

